    {
      "run": 1,
      "steps": 4,
      "narrative": "As I reflect on my time in the galley, I recall that my initial goal was to explore the space and gather information about my surroundings. I started by taking stock of my environment with a careful look around. Upon examining the galley, I noticed a kettle on the floor, which seemed out of place, and a doorway leading north and a hatch going down to the south. I also inventoried my belongings, finding that I was carrying nothing. With the kettle drawing my attention, I examined it more closely, discovering that it was made of tin and was dented on one side. Ultimately, I decided to take the kettle, likely for its potential usefulness or as a memento of my time in the galley.",
