    {
      "run": 3,
      "steps": 12,
      "narrative": "As I reflect on my time here, I remember setting out to explore the ship, starting from the cramped galley where I found a kettle and a hatch leading down to the south. My initial goal was to simply take note of my surroundings and see where I could go, so I picked up the kettle and headed north to the store. It was there that I found a coil of rope, which I examined to see that it was stiff with salt, but ultimately dropped and then picked up again.\n\nFrom the store, I continued north to the workshop, where I found an oil can on the floor. I picked that up as well, and examined it to see that it was half full, by the weight of it. However, my attempts to open the oil can were unsuccessful, as it wasn't something that could be opened. In the end, I was carrying two items: the kettle and the oil can. It was a relatively simple and uneventful exploration, but it allowed me to get a sense of the layout of the ship and the various rooms I encountered along the way.",
